          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Its awkward, formulaic delivery may bear on sincerity or depth of feeling, but it does not diminish its clear avowal form.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":3,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.86,\"reason\":\"In this occurrence, the avowal also functions as Pierre's conventional ratification of his position as Hélène's fiancé and prospective husband. The surrounding scene has already publicly treated the engagement as settled, and Pierre deliberately says what he understands must be said in that situation. Thus it is not a separately worded promise with specified terms, nor does it independently initiate the engagement, but it substantially affirms his acceptance of the marital bond and its obligations.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"The expression is not represented as a reflexive affective outburst. Pierre pauses, searches for the socially expected words, and then deliberately recalls them; the exclamation mark alone does not establish expressive discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"— Элен! — сказал он вслух и остановился.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях; но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.92,\"reason\":\"No substantial residual core force is needed beyond avowal and contextual affirmation of the engagement. Its courtship-formula function is adequately captured by T and P.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène have been left alone after her family and their guests have publicly treated them as engaged. Pierre, holding the hand of the woman the narration now calls his fiancée, struggles to produce the expected declaration, recalls the conventional words, and says them directly to her. The utterance sounds inadequate to him rather than spontaneous or triumphant.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal declaration substantially affirms Pierre's acceptance of the already socially announced engagement and positions him as bound to Hélène as her fiancé and prospective husband. Prince Vasily's blessing and announcement are separate speech acts, but they establish the situation in which Pierre's own formula operates as ratification rather than as an isolated report of feeling. Hélène's prior kiss and continued participation support practical uptake, and the supplied passage reports their marriage a month and a half later. The precise obligations are not verbalized in the target, and Pierre's dread, passivity, shame, attraction, and internal claim that he loves her make the evidence of genuine affection ambivalent rather than clearly absent.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"I recognize the supplied passage as an excerpt from Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace. The classification above relies only on the supplied evidence.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage gives strong evidence for the utterance's avowal form and engagement context, but it does not conclusively settle the depth or sincerity of Pierre's love. His attraction and internal statement support affection, while his fear, social pressure, formulaic wording, and shame complicate it. No omitted context is assumed to be absent from the work.\"}"
        }
